From: kakwa <carpentier.pf@gmail.com>
Subject: Fix smithay-client-toolkit patch version mismatch for offline chroot build
The workspace declares a `[patch."https://github.com/smithay/client-toolkit.git"]`
section that maps `sctk` to `smithay-client-toolkit` version 0.20.0 from the
crates.io registry.

No crate in the workspace actually depends on the git URL
`https://github.com/smithay/client-toolkit.git`, so the patch is unused by
normal resolution. However, the Debian cargo wrapper replaces the crates.io
registry with the Debian-provided one, where the packaged
`smithay-client-toolkit` is 0.19.2. Cargo then validates the (unused) patch
entry against the patched registry and fails the build with:

  error: patch `smithay-client-toolkit` version mismatch
  note: patch location contains version `0.19.2`, but patch definition
        requires `^0.20.0`

Since the patch matches no dependency, removing it changes the resolved
dependency graph in no way and unblocks the offline chroot build.
---
 Cargo.toml | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -80,9 +80,6 @@
 # iced_futures = { git = "https://github.com/pop-os/libcosmic//", branch = "theme-v2" }
 
-[patch."https://github.com/smithay/client-toolkit.git"]
-sctk = { package = "smithay-client-toolkit", version = "0.20.0" }
-
 [patch."https://github.com/pop-os/cosmic-protocols"]
 cosmic-protocols = { git = "https://github.com/pop-os/cosmic-protocols//", rev = "c0cff4d" }
 cosmic-client-toolkit = { git = "https://github.com/pop-os/cosmic-protocols//", rev = "c0cff4d" }
